{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Hallelujah. Happy the man</b> — \"Hallelujah\" is the poet's word, like mine, and he said: Happy the man who fears YHWH, who keeps his soul from negative commandments — not on account of his nature, or fear of a king, or because of reproach and disgrace, but only on account of his fear of HaShem, blessed be He." "<b>In His commandments he delights greatly</b> — these are positive commandments." "And the meaning of \"greatly\" — for with all his strength he acts."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 112, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:28.539075449Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}